NAME
       mkdir - create directories

SYNOPSIS
       mkdir [-p] [-m mode] dir ...

DESCRIPTION
       Creates each DIRECTORY. Without -p it is an error if the
       directory already exists or its parent does not.

OPTIONS
       -m M   set the mode of the new directory (octal, as in chmod)
       -p     create missing parents, and stay silent if the directory
              already exists
       -v     verbose (accepted, currently has no effect)

EXAMPLES
       mkdir -p /mnt/data/2026/logs

SEE ALSO
       rmdir(1), chmod(1)
